WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:05.490
So ABC's Martha Raddatz interviewed some Trump
supporters who I guess are covid, skeptical,

00:00:05.490 --> 00:00:11.400
mask's, skeptical and just generally not very
informed people.

00:00:11.400 --> 00:00:12.809
And it's really bad.

00:00:12.809 --> 00:00:17.730
And there's is a huge controversy that has
surfaced as to whether this is even something

00:00:17.730 --> 00:00:19.560
that should have been done at all.

00:00:19.560 --> 00:00:24.400
I'm going to play a clip for you here and
then we'll talk about it.

00:00:24.400 --> 00:00:27.189
It's important to understand these are not
just Trump supporters.

00:00:27.189 --> 00:00:31.349
These are Trump supporters who downplay the
pandemic to some degree, who either refuse

00:00:31.349 --> 00:00:33.830
to wear masks or don't think it's quite so
serious.

00:00:33.830 --> 00:00:38.450
And remember, we now regularly are having
over 150000 cases a day.

00:00:38.450 --> 00:00:41.460
We're back up to 1500 deaths per day.

00:00:41.460 --> 00:00:46.770
These are folks who aren't so sure it's serious,
even though more than 250000 Americans have

00:00:46.770 --> 00:00:47.770
already died.

00:00:47.770 --> 00:00:48.770
Let's take a look.

00:00:48.770 --> 00:00:53.480
Eriksson's in the aftermath of the election,
I found many who continue to downplay the

00:00:53.480 --> 00:00:54.480
pandemic.

00:00:54.480 --> 00:00:57.780
Do you not wear a mask because Donald Trump?

00:00:57.780 --> 00:00:58.840
No, absolutely not.

00:00:58.840 --> 00:01:00.750
No, because that's that's that's.

00:01:00.750 --> 00:01:01.750
I just don't believe in.

00:01:01.750 --> 00:01:02.750
Same thing with me.

00:01:02.750 --> 00:01:08.010
I mean, can the masks really defend a microbe
coming through the weaving of the fiber?

00:01:08.010 --> 00:01:09.010
I doubt it.

00:01:09.010 --> 00:01:10.300
I really doubt it.

00:01:10.300 --> 00:01:12.890
You guys just not believe the scientists on
this?

00:01:12.890 --> 00:01:15.040
No, I believe covid covered.

00:01:15.040 --> 00:01:17.670
It's real and covered is absolutely right.

00:01:17.670 --> 00:01:18.890
Just like I said, I just lost my cousin.

00:01:18.890 --> 00:01:25.500
You know, I never thought that the disease
was worth all the precautions and everything

00:01:25.500 --> 00:01:28.560
that went down as far as shutting down the
country.

00:01:28.560 --> 00:01:31.310
Even though you're worried about this virus,
how do you feed your family?

00:01:31.310 --> 00:01:34.830
I'm more worried about that than I am about
catching something that has like was a ninety

00:01:34.830 --> 00:01:37.480
seven point nine five percent survival rate.

00:01:37.480 --> 00:01:40.670
Wash your hands, eat well, take probiotics
and your vitamins.

00:01:40.670 --> 00:01:44.590
You know, just do what we do during cold and
flu season and just pray for the best.

00:01:44.590 --> 00:01:47.890
OK, so I don't believe in masks.

00:01:47.890 --> 00:01:48.890
What does that mean?

00:01:48.890 --> 00:01:50.640
You don't believe they exist?

00:01:50.640 --> 00:01:52.140
You don't believe that they do anything?

00:01:52.140 --> 00:01:55.770
Oh, well, then I don't believe masks work.

00:01:55.770 --> 00:01:57.200
Based on what?

00:01:57.200 --> 00:02:01.420
And that's my complaint with this, because
there's been this huge controversy over the

00:02:01.420 --> 00:02:04.860
responsibility or irresponsibility of platforming
these people.

00:02:04.860 --> 00:02:10.440
The idea being we know dumb people exist,
we know ignorant people exist.

00:02:10.440 --> 00:02:16.160
We know, you know, a hyper partizan people
exist who will believe anything Trump says.

00:02:16.160 --> 00:02:19.310
And what are we really getting out of this?

00:02:19.310 --> 00:02:22.510
I have talked before about the term responsible
platforming.

00:02:22.510 --> 00:02:29.910
I've interviewed Trump supporters, support,
you know, white nationalists, homophobes,

00:02:29.910 --> 00:02:30.980
whatever.

00:02:30.980 --> 00:02:37.170
My view has always been, you have to do it
responsibly where if you're going to air people

00:02:37.170 --> 00:02:43.780
saying irresponsible things, they must be
made to appear irresponsible and ignorant

00:02:43.780 --> 00:02:44.780
and unhinged.

00:02:44.780 --> 00:02:46.349
And sometimes it's a matter of just asking
questions.

00:02:46.349 --> 00:02:47.349
Right.

00:02:47.349 --> 00:02:51.180
If you're going to do this, you have to follow
up the question.

00:02:51.180 --> 00:02:55.650
When someone says, I don't believe masks work,
you say, how did you determine that masks

00:02:55.650 --> 00:02:56.860
don't work?

00:02:56.860 --> 00:02:59.240
Why do you know more than epidemiologists?

00:02:59.240 --> 00:03:00.240
What is your job?

00:03:00.240 --> 00:03:01.310
What is your education?

00:03:01.310 --> 00:03:06.170
The woman who says, you know, take your probiotics
and your vitamins and pray to God that you

00:03:06.170 --> 00:03:07.959
don't get the virus.

00:03:07.959 --> 00:03:09.630
Why do you need prayer?

00:03:09.630 --> 00:03:11.720
If probiotics and vitamins work?

00:03:11.720 --> 00:03:15.130
What evidence do you have that probiotics
and vitamins prevent coronavirus?

00:03:15.130 --> 00:03:21.380
If you need the probiotics and vitamins, why
is it that you also need to pray?

00:03:21.380 --> 00:03:22.380
Right?

00:03:22.380 --> 00:03:23.380
I mean, come on, guys.

00:03:23.380 --> 00:03:26.030
I actually question doing this.

00:03:26.030 --> 00:03:29.569
If you're not going to provide that environment.

00:03:29.569 --> 00:03:36.370
We know there are dumb people out there, but
what we are doing here, if you don't do this

00:03:36.370 --> 00:03:41.209
responsibly, the way it should be done is
you are giving these people credibility as

00:03:41.209 --> 00:03:48.670
legitimate participants among adult conversations
when they're not, you know, people who think

00:03:48.670 --> 00:03:53.200
if you cut taxes for the rich, it stimulates
the economy.

00:03:53.200 --> 00:03:56.030
That's a topic that's worthy of a discussion.

00:03:56.030 --> 00:03:57.430
Even if they are wrong.

00:03:57.430 --> 00:04:01.650
There's, you know, a legitimate debate there.

00:04:01.650 --> 00:04:06.260
They're wrong, but it's not irresponsible
the way this is irresponsible.

00:04:06.260 --> 00:04:09.280
This is like disaster porn.

00:04:09.280 --> 00:04:14.850
But what's the point if you're not going to
ostracize these people or give them enough

00:04:14.850 --> 00:04:18.839
rope to ostracize themselves, so to speak,
especially since Trump lost.

00:04:18.839 --> 00:04:22.960
And so I'm not going to play more clips because
you clearly get the picture of this.

00:04:22.960 --> 00:04:28.300
I don't want to give these people more attention,
but of course, I have no problem interviewing

00:04:28.300 --> 00:04:31.520
dumb people or even people with dangerous
or bad ideas.

00:04:31.520 --> 00:04:33.539
I've done it many, many times.

00:04:33.539 --> 00:04:37.879
But to do it, you have to do it responsibly
and you have to actually be giving these people

00:04:37.879 --> 00:04:40.379
the right rope with which they would hang
themselves.

00:04:40.379 --> 00:04:44.979
When the woman says prayer and probiotics
and vitamins, you've got to be there and say,

00:04:44.979 --> 00:04:46.279
would prayer alone work?

00:04:46.279 --> 00:04:48.400
Why have so many Christians died?

00:04:48.400 --> 00:04:49.719
Did they not pray hard enough?

00:04:49.719 --> 00:04:50.719
What's the role of prayer?

00:04:50.719 --> 00:04:53.009
Does it work to prevent other diseases like
cancer?

00:04:53.009 --> 00:04:58.550
Could prayer prevent a car accident or cause
you to regrow a limb that had to be amputated?

00:04:58.550 --> 00:04:59.550
You have to be an.

00:04:59.550 --> 00:05:04.969
Actually ready and when when you know, when
the guys say, I don't think the masks are

00:05:04.969 --> 00:05:11.300
justified based on the risk, ask if they wear
seat belts, do you pay attention to food expiration

00:05:11.300 --> 00:05:12.300
dates?

00:05:12.300 --> 00:05:16.409
Explain how they came to these conclusions,
whether they even reasoned their way in or

00:05:16.409 --> 00:05:18.089
not, because they didn't.

00:05:18.089 --> 00:05:22.039
These are people who, upon the latest questioning,
fall apart.

00:05:22.039 --> 00:05:24.970
That's what I regret that Martha Raddatz didn't
do.

00:05:24.970 --> 00:05:27.930
Had she done it, I would have been completely
on board with this segment.

00:05:27.930 --> 00:05:29.239
Sadly, she handled it in a different way.

